1
00:00:01,020 --> 00:00:02,678
Welcome to Roadmap Builder.

2
00:00:02,678 --> 00:00:04,521
It gives you a whole programme

3
00:00:04,521 --> 00:00:06,671
in one intuitive, interactive view,

4
00:00:06,671 --> 00:00:09,066
and it all runs in an ordinary browser.

5
00:00:11,020 --> 00:00:13,917
Over the next few minutes we will take the full tour,

6
00:00:13,917 --> 00:00:15,229
in eight short chapters,

7
00:00:15,229 --> 00:00:18,618
using a made-up programme so you can see how it fits together.

8
00:00:21,287 --> 00:00:23,601
Let's begin with the simplest thing you can do

9
00:00:23,601 --> 00:00:25,412
with a roadmap, which is to read it.

10
00:00:27,554 --> 00:00:29,250
This is our sample programme.

11
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:31,942
Each coloured band on the left is a workstream

12
00:00:31,942 --> 00:00:33,755
with its activities beneath it,

13
00:00:33,755 --> 00:00:35,452
and time runs across the top,

14
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:38,085
so you can see at a glance what happens when.

15
00:00:39,454 --> 00:00:41,740
When you want to know more about something,

16
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:42,644
just point at it.

17
00:00:42,644 --> 00:00:44,504
A small card appears with its dates

18
00:00:44,504 --> 00:00:46,046
and any note the author left.

19
00:00:48,887 --> 00:00:50,955
If the card is in your way, pick it up

20
00:00:50,955 --> 00:00:51,608
and move it.

21
00:00:51,608 --> 00:00:53,730
It keeps opening in the spot you chose,

22
00:00:53,730 --> 00:00:55,852
which is handy when you are presenting.

23
00:00:57,720 --> 00:00:59,724
For the full story, click the bar.

24
00:00:59,724 --> 00:01:00,549
A dialog opens

25
00:01:00,549 --> 00:01:03,143
with everything written about that activity.

26
00:01:07,554 --> 00:01:10,425
Longer programmes run off the bottom of the screen,

27
00:01:10,425 --> 00:01:12,395
so the schedule scrolls on its own.

28
00:01:12,395 --> 00:01:13,577
Notice that the years

29
00:01:13,577 --> 00:01:15,041
and the headings stay put.

30
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:22,628
Back at the top, move across the timeline.

31
00:01:22,628 --> 00:01:24,521
A faint line follows your pointer

32
00:01:24,521 --> 00:01:26,986
and tells you the exact date underneath it.

33
00:01:29,554 --> 00:01:31,969
When you only care about the big picture,

34
00:01:31,969 --> 00:01:33,265
collapse a workstream.

35
00:01:33,265 --> 00:01:35,975
Its activities fold away into one summary bar.

36
00:01:40,587 --> 00:01:41,419
Open it again,

37
00:01:41,419 --> 00:01:43,737
and try dragging the year scale itself.

38
00:01:43,737 --> 00:01:46,056
The timeline stretches under your hand,

39
00:01:46,056 --> 00:01:48,195
so you can zoom in on a busy period.

40
00:01:51,787 --> 00:01:54,156
And if you want one row to fill the screen,

41
00:01:54,156 --> 00:01:55,808
right-click it and choose fit.

42
00:01:55,808 --> 00:01:59,004
The timeline scales so that row sits neatly in the middle.

43
00:02:02,020 --> 00:02:04,253
There is a shortcut to everything, too.

44
00:02:04,253 --> 00:02:06,314
Press Control K, type a word or two,

45
00:02:06,314 --> 00:02:07,631
and pick from the list.

46
00:02:07,631 --> 00:02:09,921
Here it takes us straight back to today.

47
00:02:12,387 --> 00:02:13,886
Reading is only half of it.

48
00:02:13,886 --> 00:02:15,329
Next, let's change things,

49
00:02:15,329 --> 00:02:18,992
and you will see that editing happens right where you are looking.

50
00:02:21,954 --> 00:02:22,887
Switch to Edit,

51
00:02:22,887 --> 00:02:25,314
and the roadmap quietly becomes a form.

52
00:02:25,314 --> 00:02:25,936
Every name

53
00:02:25,936 --> 00:02:29,048
and every date turns into a field you can type in.

54
00:02:31,587 --> 00:02:33,834
To rename an activity, click its name

55
00:02:33,834 --> 00:02:34,381
and type.

56
00:02:34,381 --> 00:02:36,568
There is no save button to remember.

57
00:02:36,568 --> 00:02:38,329
The change is kept as you go.

58
00:02:39,954 --> 00:02:41,307
Dates work the same way.

59
00:02:41,307 --> 00:02:43,054
Change a start date in the row,

60
00:02:43,054 --> 00:02:46,437
and you can watch the bar slide along the timeline to match.

61
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:52,059
Adding work is just as quick.

62
00:02:52,059 --> 00:02:54,097
Type a name in the highlighted row

63
00:02:54,097 --> 00:02:55,057
and press Enter,

64
00:02:55,057 --> 00:02:56,975
then keep typing to add another.

65
00:02:56,975 --> 00:02:58,894
It feels like filling in a list.

66
00:03:01,154 --> 00:03:03,095
New activities start without dates,

67
00:03:03,095 --> 00:03:06,367
because you often know the work before you know the timing.

68
00:03:06,367 --> 00:03:08,807
When you are ready, click the row's timeline

69
00:03:08,807 --> 00:03:10,138
and the bar lands there.

70
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:14,810
Sometimes you only know when something begins.

71
00:03:14,810 --> 00:03:17,032
Give it a start date and nothing else,

72
00:03:17,032 --> 00:03:18,318
and its bar fades out,

73
00:03:18,318 --> 00:03:21,008
an honest way of saying the end is still open.

74
00:03:23,220 --> 00:03:26,207
These chips decide what is written beside each bar.

75
00:03:26,207 --> 00:03:28,725
Turn on Activity, and every bar is labelled

76
00:03:28,725 --> 00:03:29,545
with its name.

77
00:03:31,787 --> 00:03:34,046
And if a row is not ready to be seen,

78
00:03:34,046 --> 00:03:34,901
click its eye.

79
00:03:34,901 --> 00:03:37,527
The row dims here so you can still find it,

80
00:03:37,527 --> 00:03:39,664
the eye stays exactly where it was,

81
00:03:39,664 --> 00:03:41,618
and the row disappears from View

82
00:03:41,618 --> 00:03:43,388
and from anything you export.

83
00:03:45,854 --> 00:03:47,773
Quick changes happen on the chart.

84
00:03:47,773 --> 00:03:50,368
For everything else, there is one place to go,

85
00:03:50,368 --> 00:03:51,553
the Properties panel.

86
00:03:54,621 --> 00:03:55,387
Click any bar,

87
00:03:55,387 --> 00:03:58,505
and all of its settings appear in the panel on the right.

88
00:03:58,505 --> 00:04:00,310
The details sit beside the chart,

89
00:04:00,310 --> 00:04:01,240
not on top of it.

90
00:04:03,321 --> 00:04:04,276
Change the colour,

91
00:04:04,276 --> 00:04:06,133
and the bar repaints straight away,

92
00:04:06,133 --> 00:04:08,415
so you can try a few until one looks right.

93
00:04:11,887 --> 00:04:14,240
This is where you write the hover card too.

94
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:16,428
It is plain text with simple formatting,

95
00:04:16,428 --> 00:04:19,601
and the preview underneath shows exactly how it will read.

96
00:04:24,087 --> 00:04:26,209
Close the settings when you are done.

97
00:04:26,209 --> 00:04:29,076
And remember you can simply drag a bar to move it.

98
00:04:29,076 --> 00:04:31,714
It snaps to whole months, so things stay tidy.

99
00:04:34,521 --> 00:04:36,912
Dragging an edge changes how long it runs.

100
00:04:36,912 --> 00:04:40,899
That is often faster than typing a date when you are sketching a plan.

101
00:04:43,754 --> 00:04:45,780
Not everything is a stretch of work.

102
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:48,145
Right-click a bar and make it a milestone,

103
00:04:48,145 --> 00:04:51,297
and it becomes a single diamond on the day that matters.

104
00:04:53,621 --> 00:04:54,672
Changed your mind?

105
00:04:54,672 --> 00:04:56,833
Undo steps back through what you did,

106
00:04:56,833 --> 00:04:58,060
one change at a time,

107
00:04:58,060 --> 00:04:59,695
so it is safe to experiment.

108
00:05:03,787 --> 00:05:05,671
When you want more room for the chart,

109
00:05:05,671 --> 00:05:07,802
the Properties button tucks the panel away,

110
00:05:07,802 --> 00:05:09,587
and brings it back when you need it.

111
00:05:12,821 --> 00:05:14,970
Further down, set the size of the labels

112
00:05:14,970 --> 00:05:16,475
and of the dates separately.

113
00:05:16,475 --> 00:05:18,786
Here the names grow while the dates shrink,

114
00:05:18,786 --> 00:05:21,097
which suits a screen at the back of a room.

115
00:05:24,687 --> 00:05:26,404
The header has its own settings.

116
00:05:26,404 --> 00:05:27,744
Choose a size and a font,

117
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:29,032
and the heading follows.

118
00:05:31,187 --> 00:05:33,705
There is a date chip in the corner of the header.

119
00:05:33,705 --> 00:05:35,863
If you would rather not show it, untick it

120
00:05:35,863 --> 00:05:36,634
and it is gone.

121
00:05:39,754 --> 00:05:41,740
Bring it back, and look at Timeline.

122
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:43,670
Ask for six years instead of eight,

123
00:05:43,670 --> 00:05:45,600
and the whole scale redraws to fit.

124
00:05:48,054 --> 00:05:49,585
A roadmap is more than bars.

125
00:05:49,585 --> 00:05:52,209
Let's look at the notes you can add around them,

126
00:05:52,209 --> 00:05:54,724
and at making the whole thing look like yours.

127
00:05:58,721 --> 00:06:01,742
Floating cards are notes that sit on top of the chart.

128
00:06:01,742 --> 00:06:04,260
Drag one to wherever it tells the story best.

129
00:06:08,921 --> 00:06:11,291
Each card is pinned to the row it sits on.

130
00:06:11,291 --> 00:06:13,831
Watch as we hide two rows and switch to View.

131
00:06:13,831 --> 00:06:15,750
The cards move up with their rows,

132
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,951
so they still point at the right thing.

133
00:06:22,687 --> 00:06:23,464
Back in Edit,

134
00:06:23,464 --> 00:06:26,092
there is a second kind of card on the right,

135
00:06:26,092 --> 00:06:28,242
good for principles or key messages.

136
00:06:28,242 --> 00:06:30,332
Click a title and simply retype it.

137
00:06:34,187 --> 00:06:36,506
The pencil opens the rest of the card.

138
00:06:36,506 --> 00:06:39,617
The text uses the same simple formatting as before,

139
00:06:39,617 --> 00:06:41,630
and the card updates as you type.

140
00:06:47,487 --> 00:06:50,310
The heading of this group is yours to name as well.

141
00:06:50,310 --> 00:06:51,638
Rename it in Properties,

142
00:06:51,638 --> 00:06:53,797
and the tab at the top changes with it.

143
00:06:57,587 --> 00:06:59,439
Rows can be shorter or taller.

144
00:06:59,439 --> 00:07:01,413
Compact fits more on the screen,

145
00:07:01,413 --> 00:07:02,401
and a taller row

146
00:07:02,401 --> 00:07:05,980
with thicker bars makes a simple view for a few big items.

147
00:07:10,154 --> 00:07:12,292
The header comes in several styles.

148
00:07:12,292 --> 00:07:14,186
Each one is a single slim line,

149
00:07:14,186 --> 00:07:16,079
so the roadmap keeps the space.

150
00:07:18,121 --> 00:07:19,133
Now for the look.

151
00:07:19,133 --> 00:07:21,811
Tick rounded cards, and every corner softens.

152
00:07:21,811 --> 00:07:24,668
It is a small change that shifts the whole feel.

153
00:07:26,654 --> 00:07:27,906
Prefer a dark screen?

154
00:07:27,906 --> 00:07:28,919
Switch the theme,

155
00:07:28,919 --> 00:07:30,766
and the entire roadmap follows.

156
00:07:33,087 --> 00:07:35,733
And when you are not sure what colours to use,

157
00:07:35,733 --> 00:07:37,170
let the app suggest some.

158
00:07:37,170 --> 00:07:39,988
Randomise colours gives every workstream a fresh,

159
00:07:39,988 --> 00:07:40,850
matched colour.

160
00:07:44,487 --> 00:07:46,380
Press it again for another idea,

161
00:07:46,380 --> 00:07:47,799
then flip back to light.

162
00:07:47,799 --> 00:07:50,164
Each set is chosen to read well in both,

163
00:07:50,164 --> 00:07:52,825
and Undo takes you back to where you started.

164
00:07:55,288 --> 00:07:58,213
Sometimes it is quicker to edit a plan as text.

165
00:07:58,213 --> 00:08:00,578
For that, there is a live JSON editor.

166
00:08:03,855 --> 00:08:04,338
Open it,

167
00:08:04,338 --> 00:08:06,815
and it takes the left side of the screen.

168
00:08:06,815 --> 00:08:08,930
Every activity is one numbered line

169
00:08:08,930 --> 00:08:10,561
with its start and its end,

170
00:08:10,561 --> 00:08:12,616
so the whole plan is easy to scan.

171
00:08:15,955 --> 00:08:17,067
Retype an end date,

172
00:08:17,067 --> 00:08:19,760
and the bar on the right shortens as you type.

173
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:22,219
The two views are always the same roadmap.

174
00:08:24,821 --> 00:08:26,283
Names work the same way.

175
00:08:26,283 --> 00:08:27,258
Change one here,

176
00:08:27,258 --> 00:08:29,085
and its row updates beside it.

177
00:08:33,188 --> 00:08:35,231
To add an activity, just add a line.

178
00:08:35,231 --> 00:08:37,444
A moment later it appears on the chart,

179
00:08:37,444 --> 00:08:39,430
in the workstream you put it under.

180
00:08:42,221 --> 00:08:43,641
Typing mistakes happen.

181
00:08:43,641 --> 00:08:45,678
When they do, nothing is changed.

182
00:08:45,678 --> 00:08:47,468
The editor says what is wrong

183
00:08:47,468 --> 00:08:48,641
and marks the line,

184
00:08:48,641 --> 00:08:51,234
so your roadmap is never left half broken.

185
00:08:52,221 --> 00:08:54,218
Put it right, and the message clears.

186
00:08:54,218 --> 00:08:56,484
The roadmap and the text are back in step.

187
00:08:57,621 --> 00:08:59,404
Press Control S to tidy up.

188
00:08:59,404 --> 00:09:01,649
The text is laid out neatly again,

189
00:09:01,649 --> 00:09:04,422
and the line we added is given its own id.

190
00:09:07,521 --> 00:09:08,796
Cards are in here too.

191
00:09:08,796 --> 00:09:10,360
Retype a title in the text,

192
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:12,850
and the card on the chart changes to match.

193
00:09:15,322 --> 00:09:17,190
Real programmes have structure.

194
00:09:17,190 --> 00:09:18,878
Work sits inside other work,

195
00:09:18,878 --> 00:09:21,289
and some things have to wait for others.

196
00:09:21,289 --> 00:09:23,037
Roadmap Builder handles both.

197
00:09:28,055 --> 00:09:30,063
To put one activity under another,

198
00:09:30,063 --> 00:09:31,953
click its name and press Control

199
00:09:31,953 --> 00:09:33,666
and the right square bracket.

200
00:09:33,666 --> 00:09:35,496
The row above becomes a parent,

201
00:09:35,496 --> 00:09:37,977
and its bar now spans the rows beneath it.

202
00:09:41,689 --> 00:09:43,963
A parent has a small arrow of its own.

203
00:09:43,963 --> 00:09:46,656
Fold its rows away when you want the summary,

204
00:09:46,656 --> 00:09:49,349
and open them again when you want the detail.

205
00:09:49,349 --> 00:09:51,025
You can go four levels deep.

206
00:09:53,355 --> 00:09:55,071
Now for what waits for what.

207
00:09:55,071 --> 00:09:55,990
Point at a bar,

208
00:09:55,990 --> 00:09:58,318
and a line shows what it is linked to.

209
00:09:58,318 --> 00:10:00,524
The lines stay hidden until you ask,

210
00:10:00,524 --> 00:10:02,545
so a busy roadmap stays readable.

211
00:10:04,955 --> 00:10:06,763
When you do want the whole picture,

212
00:10:06,763 --> 00:10:09,604
the Links eye above the table shows every line at once.

213
00:10:14,355 --> 00:10:15,196
To add a link,

214
00:10:15,196 --> 00:10:19,579
drag from the dot at the end of a bar to the row that has to wait for it.

215
00:10:19,579 --> 00:10:20,960
An arrow joins the two.

216
00:10:24,722 --> 00:10:29,091
Now watch what happens if that activity is moved so it starts too early.

217
00:10:29,091 --> 00:10:30,244
The line turns red.

218
00:10:30,244 --> 00:10:32,065
Nothing else is moved for you.

219
00:10:32,065 --> 00:10:33,764
It is a warning, not a rule.

220
00:10:35,989 --> 00:10:38,278
Undo puts it back, and the warning clears.

221
00:10:42,789 --> 00:10:45,636
And you do not have to start from an empty page.

222
00:10:45,636 --> 00:10:47,831
Templates offers a simple, a typical,

223
00:10:47,831 --> 00:10:49,136
and a complex roadmap.

224
00:10:49,136 --> 00:10:50,560
This is the complex one,

225
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:52,220
with three levels of nesting

226
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:54,178
and linked activities throughout.

227
00:10:56,656 --> 00:10:58,854
A roadmap earns its keep in a meeting.

228
00:10:58,854 --> 00:11:00,937
So here are two ways to present one.

229
00:11:07,123 --> 00:11:09,295
The first is to steer with the pointer.

230
00:11:09,295 --> 00:11:11,133
Select the target on the toolbar.

231
00:11:11,133 --> 00:11:13,807
While the pointer is in the middle of the chart,

232
00:11:13,807 --> 00:11:14,587
nothing moves.

233
00:11:20,189 --> 00:11:21,426
Move towards an edge,

234
00:11:21,426 --> 00:11:23,370
and the timeline glides that way,

235
00:11:23,370 --> 00:11:24,902
faster the closer you get.

236
00:11:24,902 --> 00:11:26,316
Come back to the middle,

237
00:11:26,316 --> 00:11:27,671
and it eases to a stop.

238
00:11:31,789 --> 00:11:34,030
The second way is to prepare slides.

239
00:11:34,030 --> 00:11:35,835
Press Escape, switch to Edit,

240
00:11:35,835 --> 00:11:37,329
and open the Slides tab.

241
00:11:37,329 --> 00:11:40,192
Each card here is a saved view of the roadmap.

242
00:11:43,323 --> 00:11:45,902
Set the roadmap up the way you want it seen,

243
00:11:45,902 --> 00:11:47,661
then save that view as a slide

244
00:11:47,661 --> 00:11:48,833
and give it a title.

245
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:50,357
A description is optional.

246
00:11:55,856 --> 00:11:56,609
Back in View,

247
00:11:56,609 --> 00:11:58,521
select the screen on the toolbar.

248
00:11:58,521 --> 00:12:01,013
The presentation starts at the first slide,

249
00:12:01,013 --> 00:12:04,780
and a thin bar across the very top shows how far through you are.

250
00:12:10,323 --> 00:12:11,837
The right arrow moves on,

251
00:12:11,837 --> 00:12:15,712
and the roadmap glides smoothly from one saved view to the next,

252
00:12:15,712 --> 00:12:18,317
folding and opening workstreams as it goes.

253
00:12:21,256 --> 00:12:22,646
The left arrow goes back,

254
00:12:22,646 --> 00:12:24,369
and the bar at the top follows.

255
00:12:27,323 --> 00:12:28,903
When the meeting is over,

256
00:12:28,903 --> 00:12:30,610
export the slides as a PDF.

257
00:12:30,610 --> 00:12:32,633
You get one page for each slide,

258
00:12:32,633 --> 00:12:35,477
with its description as a caption underneath.

259
00:12:37,956 --> 00:12:41,265
A roadmap is only useful when other people can see it.

260
00:12:41,265 --> 00:12:42,980
So, finally, let's share it.

261
00:12:45,889 --> 00:12:47,840
Everything you need is under Export.

262
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:49,249
There are several formats,

263
00:12:49,249 --> 00:12:50,712
depending on who it is for.

264
00:12:52,256 --> 00:12:54,375
The roadmap file is your master copy.

265
00:12:54,375 --> 00:12:55,521
It holds everything,

266
00:12:55,521 --> 00:12:57,239
and it is what you would keep,

267
00:12:57,239 --> 00:13:00,275
or hand to a colleague who wants to carry on editing.

268
00:13:02,756 --> 00:13:05,124
For someone who just needs to open it,

269
00:13:05,124 --> 00:13:06,682
export a standalone page.

270
00:13:06,682 --> 00:13:09,112
That is the whole app and this roadmap,

271
00:13:09,112 --> 00:13:10,733
packed into a single file.

272
00:13:11,756 --> 00:13:13,938
Here is that file, opened on its own.

273
00:13:13,938 --> 00:13:15,649
There is no server behind it,

274
00:13:15,649 --> 00:13:17,006
and nothing to install.

275
00:13:18,523 --> 00:13:20,178
And it is still the real thing.

276
00:13:20,178 --> 00:13:21,300
The hover cards work,

277
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:24,504
and the person you sent it to can explore it for themselves.

278
00:13:30,023 --> 00:13:33,201
If you would rather they look but not change anything,

279
00:13:33,201 --> 00:13:34,967
collapse what they do not need

280
00:13:34,967 --> 00:13:36,615
and export a view-only page.

281
00:13:36,615 --> 00:13:38,498
It opens exactly as you left it,

282
00:13:38,498 --> 00:13:39,675
with no Edit button.

283
00:13:46,056 --> 00:13:46,749
For a slide,

284
00:13:46,749 --> 00:13:49,692
fit the timeline to the part you want to talk about

285
00:13:49,692 --> 00:13:51,597
and export an image of this view.

286
00:13:51,597 --> 00:13:54,251
The picture shows just what is on your screen.

287
00:13:56,956 --> 00:13:57,638
For print,

288
00:13:57,638 --> 00:14:02,073
there is a PDF that fits the whole roadmap onto a single A3 page.

289
00:14:04,856 --> 00:14:06,379
And if you ever get stuck,

290
00:14:06,379 --> 00:14:08,605
the Guide button opens a large dialog,

291
00:14:08,605 --> 00:14:11,768
with every step written down for each part of the app.

292
00:14:14,223 --> 00:14:15,553
That is Roadmap Builder.

293
00:14:15,553 --> 00:14:17,381
Your whole programme in one view,

294
00:14:17,381 --> 00:14:19,542
ready to read, to change, and to share.

